Track 1: Black Thread Stitches the Sun
- Story & Context: During the sudden midday freeze of the 2017 total eclipse over Saint Thomas, Kalan Cruz dragged an abandoned seven-foot rosewood marimba into the smoking sulfur flats just as the streetlights mistakenly flickered on at 1:14 PM. The crowd shivered in damp white linen as the percussionists attacked the wooden bars with iron-tipped mallets, unleashing a subterranean bass wobble that rattled the dentures of onlookers and drowned out nearby prayer circles with the opening toast: "Cut the gold out the sky, we tie down the light with twine." When riot police moved in with tear gas, the sudden totality plunged the field into pitch blackness, and the crowd began an undulating dembow shuffle in the freezing dark until the officers panicked and retreated into their cruisers.
